WEBVTT

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.653
Temporal incursion is complete.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:30.219
All organisms and manmade
objects have been eradicated.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.629
Probe the continuum.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.466
Has our target event
been achieved?

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.103
Negative.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:43.371
Negative target event.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.469
I don't understand, sir.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.242
We spent months making
these calculations.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.981
Time is patient...

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.919
so we must be patient with it.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.823
Eradicating a single Zahl colony

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.452
wasn't enough
for a total restoration.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.720
We have to work
on a larger scale.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.858
Take us to the Zahl homeworld.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.063
Prepare a new set
of calculations.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:14.870
We must erase
the entire species from time,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.274
every life-form...

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.800
every molecule.

00:03:11.423 --> 00:03:14.256
Space, the great unknown.

00:03:14.292 --> 00:03:17.728
Only now we're going
to know it a little better.

00:03:17.762 --> 00:03:19.127
Harry?

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.964
Before there were maps
and globes,

00:03:24.035 --> 00:03:26.401
let alone radar
and subspace sensors,

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:29.100
mariners navigated by the stars.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.199
We're returning
to that tried-and-true method,

00:03:31.242 --> 00:03:32.971
but this time,
there's a difference.

00:03:33.044 --> 00:03:35.706
Ensign Kim and Seven of Nine

00:03:35.747 --> 00:03:38.215
have merged Starfleet
and Borg ingenuity

00:03:38.249 --> 00:03:40.183
to create this new technology,

00:03:40.218 --> 00:03:43.187
and I'm sure I speak
for the entire crew

00:03:43.221 --> 00:03:45.655
when I say... thank you.

00:03:48.259 --> 00:03:51.160
Now, how the hell does it work?

00:03:52.564 --> 00:03:54.464
Astrometric sensors
measure the radiative flux

00:03:54.499 --> 00:03:56.797
of up to three billion stars
simultaneously.

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:58.769
The computer
then calculates our position

00:03:58.803 --> 00:04:00.566
relative to the center
of the galaxy.

00:04:00.605 --> 00:04:03.938
This mapping technology
is ten times more accurate

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.476
than what we've been using.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.808
Seven, will you do the honors?

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:12.847
We've plotted a new course home.

00:04:12.884 --> 00:04:14.112
By my estimates,

00:04:14.152 --> 00:04:17.178
this trajectory will eliminate
five years from your journey.

00:04:17.222 --> 00:04:18.746
Our journey.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.486
Nice work, Seven.

00:04:21.526 --> 00:04:23.790
That region of space
we're about to enter...

00:04:23.828 --> 00:04:25.955
it looks like it has
a lot of M-Class planets.

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:27.658
It does.

00:04:27.699 --> 00:04:32.534
Spatial grid 005...
primary species: The Zahl.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:34.595
What do we know
about this species?

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:37.335
Technologically advanced
but nonconfrontational.

00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:39.775
Their resistance quotient
is quite low.

00:04:39.811 --> 00:04:41.176
Thank you all for coming.

00:04:41.212 --> 00:04:42.509
We've got a lot
of work to do, so...

00:04:42.547 --> 00:04:44.981
I'd like to say a few words
if I may.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.518
I've prepared a speech
for this occasion.

00:04:47.552 --> 00:04:49.110
When I was first activated

00:04:49.154 --> 00:04:54.751
on Stardate 48315,
and I found myself

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:56.317
mano a mano
with the Delta Quadrant,

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:58.295
I didn't think
we'd survive a week

00:04:58.329 --> 00:05:00.923
let alone three years.

00:05:00.965 --> 00:05:02.296
There was strife.

00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:03.800
There was discord.

00:05:03.835 --> 00:05:05.803
You were all
at each others' throats,

00:05:05.837 --> 00:05:08.169
but over time,
I've had the pleasure and pride

00:05:08.206 --> 00:05:10.197
of watching this crew
learn to work together

00:05:10.241 --> 00:05:12.675
as colleagues, even friends.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:13.938
Here, here.

00:05:14.045 --> 00:05:14.943
Who would have thought

00:05:15.046 --> 00:05:16.536
that this eclectic group
of voyagers

00:05:16.581 --> 00:05:20.347
could actually become a family?

00:05:20.385 --> 00:05:24.344
Starfleet, Maquis, Klingon,
Talaxian, hologram, Borg,

00:05:24.389 --> 00:05:26.186
even Mr. Paris.

00:05:26.224 --> 00:05:28.215
Granted, we've had our share
of difficulties.

00:05:28.259 --> 00:05:31.285
One might say, we've seen
the best of times

00:05:31.329 --> 00:05:33.729
and the worst of times.

00:05:33.765 --> 00:05:35.198
I'd now like to recount
some of those times

00:05:35.233 --> 00:05:36.530
from my unique perspective.

00:05:36.568 --> 00:05:37.967
Under the category
of "best of times,"

00:05:38.002 --> 00:05:39.629
I invite you all to recall
the moment when I...

00:05:39.671 --> 00:05:40.660
Bridge to the Captain.

00:05:40.705 --> 00:05:42.104
Janeway here.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.199
We're being hailed...
a vessel off the port bow.

00:05:44.242 --> 00:05:45.834
On our way.

00:05:45.877 --> 00:05:47.811
Well, perhaps we could
all reconvene later.

00:05:54.319 --> 00:05:56.480
They're firing on us, Captain.

00:05:56.521 --> 00:06:00.924
It's a small vessel,
15 life-forms aboard.

00:06:00.959 --> 00:06:03.894
Low warp capacity,
limited armaments.

00:06:03.928 --> 00:06:05.190
They pose no threat.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:06.959
Open a channel.

00:06:07.999 --> 00:06:09.796
Good day, sir.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:11.859
Have we offended you
in some way?

00:06:11.903 --> 00:06:14.428
You will reverse course
immediately.

00:06:14.472 --> 00:06:16.133
This region is in dispute.

00:06:16.174 --> 00:06:18.438
You have no business
in Krenim space.

00:06:18.476 --> 00:06:19.443
I was under

00:06:19.477 --> 00:06:21.945
the impression we were
entering Zahl territory.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.244
The Zahl have
no legitimate claim here.

00:06:24.282 --> 00:06:25.772
They have taken what is ours.

00:06:25.817 --> 00:06:30.618
Reverse course...
or be destroyed.

00:06:32.857 --> 00:06:35.519
With all due respect,
unless you've got

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.289
something a little bigger
in your torpedo tubes,

00:06:37.328 --> 00:06:39.091
I'm not turning around,

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:40.757
but I'm certainly
willing to discuss

00:06:40.798 --> 00:06:42.129
this issue with you.

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:43.657
No discussion!
No compromise!

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.331
They are in retreat.

00:06:47.372 --> 00:06:48.964
His bark's obviously worse
than his bite.

00:06:49.007 --> 00:06:50.531
He seems rather intent.

00:06:50.575 --> 00:06:51.564
Let's go to Yellow Alert.

00:06:51.609 --> 00:06:52.974
Maintain our course.

00:06:53.077 --> 00:06:55.739
Maybe the Zahl
can give us some answers.

00:07:03.288 --> 00:07:05.313
As long as you travel
in Zahl territory,

00:07:05.356 --> 00:07:06.653
you travel among friends.

00:07:06.691 --> 00:07:09.489
I apologize for your mishap
with the Krenim.

00:07:09.527 --> 00:07:10.926
It was hardly traumatic.

00:07:11.029 --> 00:07:12.496
But I am curious...

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.795
the Krenim claim this region
as their own.

00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:18.529
The Krenim dominated
this space many years ago.

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:21.630
They possessed deadly weapons
based on temporal science,

00:07:21.673 --> 00:07:24.039
and it kept them in power
for a long time,

00:07:24.075 --> 00:07:25.872
but a generation ago,
we fought the Krenim.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.174
We defeated them
and took back the planets

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:29.202
that they had annexed,

00:07:29.247 --> 00:07:31.647
dismantled
their military forces.

00:07:31.683 --> 00:07:33.651
Their ships still
wander our territory

00:07:33.685 --> 00:07:35.653
making grandiose claims.

00:07:35.687 --> 00:07:36.949
Don't let them trouble you.

00:07:37.055 --> 00:07:39.956
Now, tell me about Voyager...

00:07:39.991 --> 00:07:42.892
a single ship alone,
half a galaxy from home...

00:07:42.927 --> 00:07:44.292
how exciting for you.

00:07:44.329 --> 00:07:45.387
Bridge to Captain.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.295
Sorry to interrupt,
but the Krenim vessel is back.

00:07:47.332 --> 00:07:49.129
They're demanding
to speak with you.

00:07:55.473 --> 00:07:56.804
Hello again.

00:07:56.841 --> 00:07:59.571
You've ignored our warnings,
and now you

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:01.636
consort with our enemy.

00:08:01.679 --> 00:08:03.408
Leave this space
or I'll seize your vessel

00:08:03.448 --> 00:08:04.745
and send you home
in a cargo container.

00:08:04.782 --> 00:08:06.750
Gentlemen, please.

00:08:06.784 --> 00:08:10.083
Believe me, we're not
conspiring against you.

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:13.849
Captain, there's a spatial
distortion heading toward us.

00:08:13.891 --> 00:08:15.916
Whatever it is, it's huge...
five light-years across

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.552
and it's expanding.

00:08:17.595 --> 00:08:19.187
Tracking its origin.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:21.255
A vessel
near the Zahl homeworld.

00:08:21.299 --> 00:08:22.266
What?

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.494
It appears to be

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:26.025
a massive buildup
of temporal energy...

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.504
some kind
of space-time shock wave.

00:08:28.539 --> 00:08:29.563
Tom?

00:08:29.607 --> 00:08:32.098
It's destabilizing
our warp field.

00:08:32.143 --> 00:08:33.542
I've lost engines.

00:08:33.578 --> 00:08:35.409
Shields to full.

00:08:35.446 --> 00:08:37.107
Secure primary systems.

00:08:37.148 --> 00:08:38.775
All hands brace for impact.

00:08:59.304 --> 00:09:00.703
She's dead.

00:09:00.738 --> 00:09:02.535
Shields at 17 percent.

00:09:02.573 --> 00:09:04.302
The Krenim are firing again.

00:09:04.342 --> 00:09:07.209
We're being hailed.

00:09:07.245 --> 00:09:08.212
It's about time.

00:09:08.246 --> 00:09:09.736
On screen.

00:09:09.781 --> 00:09:13.444
We've done nothing
to provoke these attacks.

00:09:13.484 --> 00:09:16.920
Your presence in our space
is provocation enough.

00:09:16.954 --> 00:09:20.014
We've been trying to communicate
with your vessels,

00:09:20.058 --> 00:09:23.152
but the only answer I get
is weapons fire.

00:09:23.194 --> 00:09:24.752
State your identity.

00:09:24.796 --> 00:09:28.288
Captain Janeway
of the Federation Starship...

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:31.928
And your reason
for violating our borders.

00:09:32.036 --> 00:09:33.560
We're simply trying
to get home.

00:09:33.604 --> 00:09:36.505
If you'd kindly allow us
to pass through...

00:09:36.541 --> 00:09:39.101
No. You will submit
to the Krenim lmperium.

00:09:39.143 --> 00:09:41.771
I would prefer
to seize your vessel

00:09:41.813 --> 00:09:44.145
before it is too badly damaged.

00:09:44.182 --> 00:09:49.279
Surrender now and I will forego
the execution of your crew.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:52.585
I don't respond well to threats.

00:09:54.258 --> 00:09:56.488
Then prepare to be boarded.

00:10:00.164 --> 00:10:04.601
All hands, battle stations.

00:10:04.635 --> 00:10:08.935
This is turning into
the week of hell.

00:10:17.515 --> 00:10:18.641
They're charging weapons.

00:10:18.683 --> 00:10:19.809
Three seconds to impact.

00:10:19.851 --> 00:10:21.785
Evasive maneuvers.

00:10:21.819 --> 00:10:24.652
Direct hit
to our secondary hull.

00:10:24.689 --> 00:10:26.350
I still don't understand
why these torpedoes

00:10:26.391 --> 00:10:27.858
are ripping
right through our shields.

00:10:33.264 --> 00:10:35.494
Their weapons are
chroniton-based.

00:10:35.533 --> 00:10:36.727
They're penetrating our shields

00:10:36.768 --> 00:10:38.463
because they're
in a state of temporal flux.

00:10:38.503 --> 00:10:41.131
Then let's exercise
the better part of valor.

00:10:41.172 --> 00:10:42.799
Get us out of here, warp 6.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:44.307
Warp 6.

00:10:44.342 --> 00:10:46.674
No sign of pursuit.

00:10:46.711 --> 00:10:47.803
Damage report.

00:10:47.845 --> 00:10:49.437
15 wounded.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:50.572
Main power is down.

00:10:50.615 --> 00:10:54.381
We've lost environmental control
on Decks 7 and 8.

00:10:54.419 --> 00:10:56.216
The computer is off-line.

00:10:56.254 --> 00:10:58.552
Mr. Kim, do we have
any sensors left?

00:10:58.589 --> 00:11:00.216
Short-range only.

00:11:00.258 --> 00:11:02.158
Commander...

00:11:03.761 --> 00:11:05.956
put the ship
on 24-hour Tactical Alert.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.964
Tuvok, analyze
whatever data we've got

00:11:08.065 --> 00:11:09.589
on those
chroniton torpedoes.

00:11:09.634 --> 00:11:12.967
See if you can
modify our shielding.

00:11:13.037 --> 00:11:16.837
When those Krenim attack again,
I want to be ready.

00:11:30.888 --> 00:11:32.685
Enter.

00:11:35.827 --> 00:11:38.125
Sir, you were correct.

00:11:38.162 --> 00:11:41.097
The Zahl homeworld
was the focal point.

00:11:41.132 --> 00:11:42.997
It's erasure has produced
a complete

00:11:43.067 --> 00:11:44.932
temporal restoration.

00:11:44.969 --> 00:11:46.698
Complete?

00:11:46.737 --> 00:11:47.761
Yes, sir.

00:11:50.441 --> 00:11:54.400
If I told you to count
the stars in the cosmos,

00:11:54.445 --> 00:11:56.310
would the task ever be complete?

00:11:57.381 --> 00:11:58.507
Sir?

00:11:58.549 --> 00:12:00.779
Our attempts may be sufficient.

00:12:00.818 --> 00:12:03.343
They may be even
relatively successful,

00:12:03.387 --> 00:12:05.321
but they will never be complete.

00:12:05.356 --> 00:12:08.154
Choose your words
with more precision.

00:12:08.192 --> 00:12:09.887
My apologies.

00:12:09.927 --> 00:12:12.225
What were the exact results?

00:12:12.263 --> 00:12:15.232
The Krenim lmperium
has been restored to power.

00:12:15.266 --> 00:12:16.893
Our territory now includes

00:12:16.934 --> 00:12:22.236
849 inhabited worlds
spanning 5,000 parsecs.

00:12:22.273 --> 00:12:23.638
Counter-indications?

00:12:23.674 --> 00:12:25.335
Negligible.

00:12:25.376 --> 00:12:26.968
No superior enemy forces.

00:12:27.078 --> 00:12:29.512
No unexpected diseases.

00:12:29.547 --> 00:12:33.381
Calculations indicate
a 98 percent restoration.

00:12:33.417 --> 00:12:36.648
Our race is thriving once again.

00:12:36.687 --> 00:12:39.451
The, uh...

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:42.687
the colony at Kyana Prime...

00:12:43.861 --> 00:12:46.329
that was restored as well?

00:12:47.365 --> 00:12:49.890
No, sir.

00:12:49.934 --> 00:12:50.901
In this timeline,

00:12:50.935 --> 00:12:53.028
the lmperium does not extend
that far.

00:12:58.776 --> 00:13:00.300
Then our mission has failed.

00:13:01.779 --> 00:13:04.407
Begin calculations
for the next incursion.

00:13:04.448 --> 00:13:07.679
Sir, we have just accomplished
the impossible...

00:13:07.718 --> 00:13:10.209
a 98 percent restoration.

00:13:10.254 --> 00:13:12.586
Another incursion,
even a minor one,

00:13:12.623 --> 00:13:14.420
could undermine everything.

00:13:14.458 --> 00:13:18.258
We should dismantle this weapon
and rejoin our people.

00:13:18.296 --> 00:13:20.662
No, not until every colony...

00:13:20.698 --> 00:13:21.824
every individual...

00:13:21.866 --> 00:13:23.800
every blade of grass
is restored.

00:13:23.834 --> 00:13:27.497
You said yourself,
our task will never be complete.

00:13:27.538 --> 00:13:32.237
Please, we should be satisfied
with what we have accomplished.

00:13:32.276 --> 00:13:35.245
For 200 years, we have
never come this close.

00:13:35.279 --> 00:13:36.906
Not close enough.

00:13:36.948 --> 00:13:38.540
If I may speak my thoughts.

00:13:39.517 --> 00:13:41.246
Many among the crew
are convinced

00:13:41.285 --> 00:13:43.253
that you have lost
your objectivity.

00:13:43.386 --> 00:13:46.116
They think your quest
for... precision

00:13:46.155 --> 00:13:47.417
is unrealistic.

00:13:49.025 --> 00:13:50.424
Sir...

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:53.395
we will never restore
100 percent of what we had.

00:13:53.429 --> 00:13:55.795
We can manipulate
the time continuum

00:13:55.832 --> 00:13:57.629
for another ten centuries...

00:13:57.667 --> 00:14:00.101
it will never happen.

00:14:01.738 --> 00:14:05.765
Return to your station and begin
a new set of calculations.

00:14:05.808 --> 00:14:08.140
Is that clear?

00:14:08.177 --> 00:14:10.407
Perfectly.

00:14:10.446 --> 00:14:12.880
You surprise me, Obrist.

00:14:14.684 --> 00:14:17.050
After so many years,

00:14:17.086 --> 00:14:20.647
you still perceive time
through conventional eyes.

00:14:21.958 --> 00:14:25.155
"Never" is a word
that has no meaning here.

00:14:25.194 --> 00:14:27.822
As long as we stay
on this vessel,

00:14:27.864 --> 00:14:31.595
protected from space-time,

00:14:31.634 --> 00:14:35.001
we have all eternity
to accomplish our mission.

00:14:38.574 --> 00:14:40.007
Of course, sir.

00:14:52.021 --> 00:14:52.988
Return fire.

00:14:53.022 --> 00:14:54.717
Weapons are down.

00:14:54.757 --> 00:14:56.987
My attempt to modify
the shielding was unsuccessful.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.721
Captain,
during that last exchange

00:14:58.761 --> 00:14:59.728
we did some damage.

00:14:59.762 --> 00:15:00.786
The Krenim's aft shields
are down.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:01.728
They're vulnerable.

00:15:01.764 --> 00:15:03.163
We've got to hit them now!

00:15:03.199 --> 00:15:04.223
With what?

00:15:04.267 --> 00:15:05.598
Phaser banks are burned out.

00:15:05.635 --> 00:15:07.159
Torpedo launchers are off-line.

00:15:07.203 --> 00:15:08.534
Doctor to Bridge.

00:15:08.571 --> 00:15:10.266
We've got
a power overload in Sick Bay.

00:15:10.306 --> 00:15:12.240
I need an engineer
down here right away.

00:15:12.275 --> 00:15:13.242
Stand by, Doctor.

00:15:13.276 --> 00:15:14.709
Harry, can you handle it
from here?

00:15:14.744 --> 00:15:15.938
No, sir.

00:15:16.045 --> 00:15:17.603
The overload's spreading.

00:15:17.647 --> 00:15:19.478
Half that deck is going
to blow in less than

00:15:19.515 --> 00:15:21.039
- five minutes.
- Doctor, get

00:15:21.084 --> 00:15:22.108
your patients out of there.

00:15:22.151 --> 00:15:23.778
All hands,
this is the Bridge.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:25.913
Emergency evacuation, Deck 5.

00:15:25.955 --> 00:15:28.219
How many torpedoes
do we have left?

00:15:28.257 --> 00:15:29.724
Eleven.

00:15:29.759 --> 00:15:31.192
Arm four of them.

00:15:31.227 --> 00:15:33.422
Stand by
to open the launch doors.

00:15:33.463 --> 00:15:35.522
We're going to deploy them
like mines.

00:15:35.565 --> 00:15:36.930
Aye, Captain.

00:15:36.966 --> 00:15:38.729
Tom, I need your finesse.

00:15:38.768 --> 00:15:42.329
Let the Krenim get
within 5,000 meters of us.

00:15:42.372 --> 00:15:43.703
No problem.

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:45.071
Keep moving.

00:15:45.108 --> 00:15:47.770
Quickly. Please, move quickly.

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:51.576
Warning. Structural collapse
in three minutes.

00:15:52.515 --> 00:15:54.107
Torpedoes armed and ready.

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:55.708
They're within range.

00:15:55.752 --> 00:15:58.118
Tuvok...

00:15:58.154 --> 00:15:59.416
do it.

00:16:09.799 --> 00:16:10.959
Got 'em!

00:16:15.605 --> 00:16:17.539
The conduits
on Deck 5 are overloading.

00:16:17.573 --> 00:16:18.904
30 seconds till they blow.

00:16:18.941 --> 00:16:20.169
Keep moving.

00:16:21.511 --> 00:16:22.773
Please, hurry.

00:16:22.812 --> 00:16:25.337
That's it.

00:16:25.381 --> 00:16:29.545
Warning. Structural collapse
in 20 seconds.

00:16:32.422 --> 00:16:33.946
15 seconds!

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:38.154
Warning. Structural collapse
in 10 seconds.

00:16:39.462 --> 00:16:42.556
Warning. Structural collapse
in five...

00:16:42.598 --> 00:16:44.088
four...

00:16:44.133 --> 00:16:46.067
three... two...

00:16:46.102 --> 00:16:47.569
one.

00:16:55.945 --> 00:16:57.674
Report!

00:16:58.714 --> 00:17:03.242
Sections 10 through 53
on Deck 5...

00:17:03.286 --> 00:17:04.446
are gone.

00:17:04.487 --> 00:17:06.011
Casualties?

00:17:06.055 --> 00:17:08.080
Reports are coming in.

00:17:08.124 --> 00:17:10.922
12 wounded...
many of them critically.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.087
The Doctor is setting up
a triage facility

00:17:13.129 --> 00:17:14.596
in the Mess Hall.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:16.598
Two crew members were killed
in the breach.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.791
Stand down Red Alert.

00:17:19.836 --> 00:17:22.805
Assemble a security team.

00:17:22.839 --> 00:17:24.306
Survey the ship deck by deck.

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:26.308
I want a full damage report.

00:17:31.214 --> 00:17:33.045
I'll be in my ready room.

00:17:34.784 --> 00:17:36.615
You have the Bridge...

00:17:36.652 --> 00:17:38.950
what's left of it.

00:17:57.273 --> 00:17:58.604
Come in.

00:17:59.909 --> 00:18:01.900
Sorry about the mess.

00:18:01.944 --> 00:18:03.878
You should see my place.

00:18:03.913 --> 00:18:06.404
They haven't looked as bad
since my old Academy days.

00:18:06.449 --> 00:18:08.383
Is there something on your mind?

00:18:08.417 --> 00:18:09.714
Yes,

00:18:09.752 --> 00:18:11.083
but you're not going to like it.

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:13.111
That's never stopped you before.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:15.614
Broken.

00:18:17.493 --> 00:18:19.358
I'll be blunt.

00:18:19.395 --> 00:18:21.920
Our strategy's failing.

00:18:22.031 --> 00:18:23.498
It was a good idea
to try and create

00:18:23.533 --> 00:18:25.262
temporal shielding,
but it isn't working.

00:18:25.301 --> 00:18:27.269
Not yet, but it will.

00:18:27.303 --> 00:18:29.203
With every attack,
we gather more information

00:18:29.238 --> 00:18:30.535
about their chroniton weapons.

00:18:30.573 --> 00:18:32.165
How many more attacks
will it take?

00:18:32.208 --> 00:18:34.403
Before long, there won't be
a ship left to protect.

00:18:35.411 --> 00:18:37.879
We don't have a choice.

00:18:37.914 --> 00:18:39.677
Maybe we do.

00:18:41.317 --> 00:18:43.683
Here comes the part
I'm not going to like.

00:18:43.719 --> 00:18:46.745
We should consider
leaving the ship behind,

00:18:46.789 --> 00:18:50.225
breaking the crew into smaller
groups... escape pods, shuttles...

00:18:50.259 --> 00:18:51.954
each one with its own course.

00:18:51.994 --> 00:18:53.825
If all goes well,
we'll rendezvous

00:18:53.863 --> 00:18:55.728
on the other side
of Krenim space.

00:18:56.766 --> 00:18:58.233
Then what?

00:18:58.267 --> 00:19:00.895
We'll cross that bridge
when we come to it,

00:19:00.937 --> 00:19:03.531
but at least we'd be increasing
our chances of survival.

00:19:07.009 --> 00:19:08.806
Abandon ship?

00:19:08.844 --> 00:19:10.869
The answer's no.

00:19:10.913 --> 00:19:13.541
I'm not breaking up
the family, Chakotay.

00:19:13.583 --> 00:19:15.414
We're stronger as a team.

00:19:15.451 --> 00:19:18.113
One crew, one ship.

00:19:18.154 --> 00:19:19.451
The moment we split apart,

00:19:19.488 --> 00:19:21.456
we lose the ability
to pool our talents.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:22.889
We become vulnerable.

00:19:22.925 --> 00:19:25.086
We'll get picked off one by one.

00:19:25.127 --> 00:19:28.995
Now, I say we make
our stand together.

00:19:31.233 --> 00:19:34.464
To be honest, I wasn't too fond
of the idea myself.

00:19:34.503 --> 00:19:36.733
As long as Voyager's
in one piece,

00:19:36.772 --> 00:19:38.967
we stay.

00:19:42.411 --> 00:19:43.639
We stay.

00:19:45.181 --> 00:19:46.910
This looks like
it stayed in one piece.

00:19:46.949 --> 00:19:48.439
Where does this go?

00:19:48.484 --> 00:19:49.883
My lucky teacup.

00:19:49.919 --> 00:19:51.318
Right over here.

00:19:51.354 --> 00:19:54.755
Red Alert.
We're under attack.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.758
Two Krenim warships
off the port bow.

00:20:11.007 --> 00:20:13.168
When are they going
to get us out of here?

00:20:13.209 --> 00:20:16.144
Try to relax.
Let's get back to the game.

00:20:16.178 --> 00:20:20.706
Grace Kelly...
cat burglars... the Riviera.

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:22.615
Name the title...

00:20:22.652 --> 00:20:24.620
and the male lead.

00:20:24.654 --> 00:20:25.985
To Catch a Thief.

00:20:26.055 --> 00:20:26.987
Right.

00:20:27.056 --> 00:20:28.250
Clark Gable.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.724
Wrong. Cary Grant.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:31.727
I've seen the holographic

00:20:31.761 --> 00:20:33.820
version twice...
it's Clark Gable.

00:20:33.863 --> 00:20:35.626
I think you're getting them
confused

00:20:35.665 --> 00:20:38.225
because they have the same
initials. It was Grant.

00:20:38.267 --> 00:20:39.734
No more
20th-century entertainment.

00:20:39.769 --> 00:20:40.736
I'm terrible at it.

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:41.828
My turn.

00:20:41.871 --> 00:20:45.170
Category... athletics.

00:20:45.207 --> 00:20:47.300
Fire away.

00:20:47.343 --> 00:20:48.605
A notorious athlete...

00:20:48.644 --> 00:20:51.169
parrises' squares,
championship finals...

00:20:51.213 --> 00:20:53.477
uh... controversial decision.

00:20:53.516 --> 00:20:55.916
M'Kota R'Cho...
the first and only Klingon

00:20:55.951 --> 00:20:57.282
to ever play the game.

00:20:57.319 --> 00:20:59.844
During the finals of 2342,
one of the referees

00:20:59.889 --> 00:21:01.789
called a penalty
against his team.

00:21:01.824 --> 00:21:03.951
R'Cho strangled him.

00:21:04.026 --> 00:21:05.288
Impressive.

00:21:05.327 --> 00:21:08.160
You're looking at a true
sports aficionado.

00:21:08.197 --> 00:21:11.189
Let's see... how about
interstellar history?

00:21:11.233 --> 00:21:13.258
Oh, great. You pick
the one subject

00:21:13.302 --> 00:21:15.133
I almost failed at the Academy.

00:21:15.171 --> 00:21:16.229
Go ahead and ask...

00:21:17.273 --> 00:21:18.240
Hey, you all right?

00:21:18.274 --> 00:21:19.241
Mm-hmm.

00:21:20.409 --> 00:21:22.309
It just...

00:21:22.344 --> 00:21:23.641
hurts a little.

00:21:27.683 --> 00:21:29.878
It feels like we've
been here for days.

00:21:29.919 --> 00:21:31.978
Actually, it's been
about six hours.

00:21:32.054 --> 00:21:34.454
Try to hang on, B'Elanna.

00:21:34.490 --> 00:21:37.482
The emergency crews are
going to find us any minute.

00:21:40.129 --> 00:21:42.290
Come on, hurry up!

00:21:43.766 --> 00:21:45.996
Go ahead and ask
your stupid question,

00:21:46.035 --> 00:21:47.002
before I pass out

00:21:47.036 --> 00:21:49.129
and you don't have
anybody to play with.

00:21:50.773 --> 00:21:52.297
Okay.

00:21:52.341 --> 00:21:55.105
Um... it's a famous ship.

00:21:55.144 --> 00:21:57.339
Uh... pre-warp civilization...

00:21:57.379 --> 00:21:59.745
um... Montana...

00:21:59.782 --> 00:22:03.878
uh... second stage
had chemical engines.

00:22:03.919 --> 00:22:05.318
Another clue.

00:22:05.354 --> 00:22:07.049
Vulcans, um...

00:22:07.089 --> 00:22:08.750
Earth... first contact.

00:22:08.791 --> 00:22:10.691
Oh, right, right.

00:22:10.726 --> 00:22:14.560
Um... uh... uh...
Zephram Cochrane's ship...

00:22:14.597 --> 00:22:16.497
What was it called?

00:22:16.532 --> 00:22:18.523
God, it's on the tip
of my tongue.

00:22:19.568 --> 00:22:20.967
Okay, okay.
Here, you better lie down now.

00:22:21.003 --> 00:22:21.970
Enough trivia for now.

00:22:22.004 --> 00:22:23.403
No.
No, I'm going to get this one.

00:22:28.844 --> 00:22:30.072
Lieutenant. Ensign.

00:22:30.112 --> 00:22:31.977
It's about time.

00:22:32.014 --> 00:22:34.073
What happened to the turbolift?

00:22:34.116 --> 00:22:35.811
During the last attack,

00:22:35.851 --> 00:22:37.978
19 main power relays
were severed.

00:22:38.087 --> 00:22:40.715
The entire turbolift system
is nonoperational.

00:22:40.756 --> 00:22:43.816
Get me to the Jefferies tube
network on Deck 11.

00:22:43.859 --> 00:22:46.589
The EPS manifold
must have taken a hit, too.

00:22:46.629 --> 00:22:48.494
Seven of Nine
can go take a look.

00:22:48.531 --> 00:22:49.998
We have to get you
to the Doctor.

00:22:50.099 --> 00:22:52.090
All right.

00:22:52.134 --> 00:22:53.101
The Phoenix.

00:22:53.135 --> 00:22:54.397
What?

00:22:54.436 --> 00:22:56.404
The correct response
to your query.

00:22:56.438 --> 00:22:58.167
The vessel Ensign Kim
was describing...

00:22:58.207 --> 00:22:59.640
it was designated the Phoenix.

00:22:59.675 --> 00:23:01.836
Not bad.
I didn't realize

00:23:01.877 --> 00:23:03.504
you knew so much
about Earth history.

00:23:03.546 --> 00:23:06.606
I don't, but the Borg were
present during those events.

00:23:06.649 --> 00:23:07.616
Really?

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:08.912
It's a complicated story.

00:23:08.951 --> 00:23:10.111
Perhaps another time.

00:23:10.152 --> 00:23:11.551
I think so.

00:23:13.088 --> 00:23:14.316
Transverse bulkheads.

00:23:14.356 --> 00:23:15.880
We've set up
emergency force fields

00:23:15.925 --> 00:23:17.825
between all decks
and every section.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:19.657
In the event
of a cataclysmic breach,

00:23:19.695 --> 00:23:21.526
most of us will be protected.

00:23:24.834 --> 00:23:26.859
Ingenious.

00:23:26.902 --> 00:23:28.836
Actually, you can thank
Mr. Paris.

00:23:28.871 --> 00:23:30.270
He came up with the idea.

00:23:30.306 --> 00:23:32.740
I was inspired
by an ancient steamship...

00:23:32.775 --> 00:23:33.969
the Titanic.

00:23:34.009 --> 00:23:35.408
The engineers of the day

00:23:35.444 --> 00:23:37.503
constructed a series
of special bulkheads...

00:23:37.546 --> 00:23:39.639
sort of like a honeycomb...

00:23:39.682 --> 00:23:41.172
that would lower into place

00:23:41.217 --> 00:23:42.741
if they suffered
a major hull breach.

00:23:42.785 --> 00:23:44.377
In theory,
they could stay afloat

00:23:44.420 --> 00:23:46.183
even with half the ship
filled with water.

00:23:46.222 --> 00:23:47.655
The Titanic?

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:49.590
As I recall, it sank.

00:23:49.625 --> 00:23:51.889
Well, let's just say,

00:23:51.927 --> 00:23:54.293
I've made a few improvements.

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:56.298
I knew your fixation
with history

00:23:56.332 --> 00:23:58.698
would come in handy someday.
Good work.

00:23:58.734 --> 00:24:00.133
Doctor to Lieutenant Paris.

00:24:00.169 --> 00:24:01.227
Go ahead, Doc.

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:02.532
Report to the Mess Hall at once.

00:24:02.571 --> 00:24:04.471
More wounded are on the way.

00:24:04.506 --> 00:24:06.406
I'll be right there.

00:24:06.442 --> 00:24:07.966
I'm a popular guy today.

00:24:47.180 --> 00:24:49.080
Seven of Nine to Tuvok.

00:24:49.115 --> 00:24:50.514
Tuvok here.

00:24:50.550 --> 00:24:52.609
There is an undetonated
chroniton torpedo

00:24:52.652 --> 00:24:54.620
lodged in the starboard
Jefferies tube

00:24:54.654 --> 00:24:56.679
on Deck 11, Section 2.

00:24:56.723 --> 00:24:59.624
The warhead is still active.

00:24:59.659 --> 00:25:01.490
Do not attempt to disarm it.

00:25:01.528 --> 00:25:04.224
Hold your position
and wait for my arrival.

00:25:04.264 --> 00:25:05.526
Is that clear?

00:25:05.565 --> 00:25:07.556
Arrive quickly.

00:25:13.640 --> 00:25:15.938
I've stopped
the internal bleeding.

00:25:15.976 --> 00:25:19.036
You're going to be okay.

00:25:19.079 --> 00:25:21.912
Is that your expert opinion?

00:25:23.450 --> 00:25:25.077
That's a promise.

00:25:28.388 --> 00:25:29.912
I know.
It still hurts.

00:25:29.956 --> 00:25:31.583
No, it's all right.

00:25:33.593 --> 00:25:36.221
You've got a ruptured vertebra.

00:25:36.263 --> 00:25:37.491
I'll see if I can repair it.

00:25:37.530 --> 00:25:39.122
Mr. Paris, your assistance,
please.

00:25:39.165 --> 00:25:40.132
Give me a minute.

00:25:40.166 --> 00:25:41.963
Now, Lieutenant.

00:25:43.803 --> 00:25:45.202
I'll be right back.

00:25:45.238 --> 00:25:47.798
Don't go anywhere.

00:25:47.841 --> 00:25:49.433
In case you hadn't noticed,

00:25:49.476 --> 00:25:51.842
B'Elanna is not
the only patient here.

00:25:51.878 --> 00:25:52.845
She's in pain.

00:25:52.879 --> 00:25:54.278
But no longer
in danger of dying.

00:25:54.314 --> 00:25:56.111
That is the first rule
of medical triage...

00:25:56.149 --> 00:25:57.480
make sure the patient will live,

00:25:57.517 --> 00:25:58.814
then move on to the next one.

00:25:58.852 --> 00:26:01.184
Emotional detachment
is essential.

00:26:01.221 --> 00:26:03.655
Otherwise, you risk
impairing your judgment.

00:26:03.690 --> 00:26:05.180
I understand.

00:26:05.225 --> 00:26:07.591
You could be seeing more
of your friends in here soon.

00:26:07.627 --> 00:26:10.824
If you can't handle it,
I'll find another assistant.

00:26:10.864 --> 00:26:12.388
You can leave.

00:26:14.567 --> 00:26:16.933
"Physician, heal thyself."

00:26:17.037 --> 00:26:20.336
What's that supposed to mean?

00:26:20.373 --> 00:26:22.102
Well, it seems to me
that you're the one

00:26:22.142 --> 00:26:23.734
who's getting emotional
around here.

00:26:28.748 --> 00:26:30.215
Several weeks ago,

00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:33.515
just before the conduits
on Deck 5 breached,

00:26:33.553 --> 00:26:35.748
I saw Ensign Strickler
and Crewman Emmanuel

00:26:35.789 --> 00:26:37.051
at the end of a corridor.

00:26:37.090 --> 00:26:40.856
They were... trying
to reach the Jefferies tube.

00:26:44.297 --> 00:26:45.662
I kept the hatch open,

00:26:45.699 --> 00:26:48.429
waited for them
as long as I could...

00:26:48.468 --> 00:26:50.459
but time ran out.

00:26:51.738 --> 00:26:55.265
I had no choice
but to seal the hatch.

00:27:00.780 --> 00:27:02.805
That must have been
very hard for you.

00:27:02.849 --> 00:27:04.840
My point is,
it could have been worse.

00:27:04.884 --> 00:27:07.785
Had I lost my objectivity,
I might have kept the hatch open

00:27:07.821 --> 00:27:09.311
and everyone
would have perished.

00:27:10.724 --> 00:27:12.214
This man has
damaged lung tissue.

00:27:12.258 --> 00:27:13.589
Treat him with inaprovaline.

00:27:16.896 --> 00:27:19.228
If we attempt
to dislodge the torpedo

00:27:19.265 --> 00:27:20.323
or move it
with the transporters,

00:27:20.367 --> 00:27:22.028
it will most likely detonate.

00:27:22.068 --> 00:27:23.160
Can we disarm it?

00:27:23.203 --> 00:27:26.070
No. The warhead
is already destabilizing.

00:27:26.106 --> 00:27:28.472
I estimate it will explode
in less than two minutes.

00:27:28.508 --> 00:27:31.739
If we reroute emergency
power to this junction,

00:27:31.778 --> 00:27:33.268
and erect a level-10
force field,

00:27:33.313 --> 00:27:35.213
it should be enough
to contain the explosion.

00:27:35.248 --> 00:27:36.215
We must hurry.

00:27:36.249 --> 00:27:37.216
If I can determine

00:27:37.250 --> 00:27:38.945
the exact temporal variance
of this torpedo,

00:27:38.985 --> 00:27:40.680
it will help us perfect
the temporal shielding.

00:27:40.720 --> 00:27:41.778
There is no time.

00:27:41.821 --> 00:27:43.755
We may never have
this opportunity again.

00:27:43.790 --> 00:27:46.554
I am giving you an order. Now!

00:27:46.593 --> 00:27:50.188
The temporal variance
is 1.47 microseconds.

00:27:50.230 --> 00:27:51.197
Excellent work.

00:27:51.231 --> 00:27:52.596
But if you disobey
my orders again,

00:27:52.632 --> 00:27:53.599
I will be forced to...

00:28:04.010 --> 00:28:08.242
Captain's Log, Stardate 51268.4.

00:28:08.281 --> 00:28:12.183
This morning's attack destroyed
the power grid on Deck 11.

00:28:12.218 --> 00:28:13.685
No casualties this time,

00:28:13.720 --> 00:28:16.518
but the replicator system
was badly damaged.

00:28:16.556 --> 00:28:19.184
We've gone to emergency rations.

00:28:19.225 --> 00:28:22.251
As a result, the situation
has gotten a little worse.

00:28:22.295 --> 00:28:25.196
Environmental controls
continue to fail.

00:28:25.231 --> 00:28:28.598
Seven decks have been rendered
uninhabitable

00:28:28.635 --> 00:28:31.399
and we've had
to relocate the crew.

00:28:31.438 --> 00:28:34.669
Quarters are close,
nerves are frayed,

00:28:34.707 --> 00:28:37.335
and I'm not sure what's
more difficult to maintain...

00:28:37.377 --> 00:28:40.505
Voyager's systems
or the crew's morale.

00:28:40.547 --> 00:28:42.947
What's important
is that we're together,

00:28:43.016 --> 00:28:47.749
working towards a single goal...
survival.

00:28:48.588 --> 00:28:50.078
Happy birthday.

00:28:50.123 --> 00:28:51.954
Happy what?

00:28:51.991 --> 00:28:54.255
Today is May 20.

00:28:57.564 --> 00:28:58.997
Is it?

00:29:00.733 --> 00:29:03.065
I thought
we were still in April.

00:29:03.103 --> 00:29:05.071
Guess I've lost track
of the time.

00:29:05.105 --> 00:29:08.541
Well, this should help.

00:29:13.680 --> 00:29:15.341
It's beautiful.

00:29:15.381 --> 00:29:17.906
19th century...
mechanical movement.

00:29:17.951 --> 00:29:19.509
It's a replica
of the chronometer

00:29:19.552 --> 00:29:21.577
worn by Captain Cray
of the British Navy.

00:29:21.621 --> 00:29:24.818
His ship was hit
by a typhoon in the Pacific.

00:29:24.858 --> 00:29:27.224
Everyone back in England
thought they were killed,

00:29:27.260 --> 00:29:29.194
but eight months later,

00:29:29.229 --> 00:29:31.891
Cray sailed his ship
into London harbor.

00:29:31.931 --> 00:29:33.592
There wasn't much left of it...

00:29:33.633 --> 00:29:37.967
a few planks, half a sail,
but he got his crew home.

00:29:41.107 --> 00:29:44.201
I appreciate the sentiment,
but I can't keep this.

00:29:44.244 --> 00:29:45.472
Recycle it.

00:29:45.512 --> 00:29:47.946
We can't afford to waste energy
on nonessentials.

00:29:48.014 --> 00:29:51.279
Kathryn, I replicated this
months ago.

00:29:51.317 --> 00:29:52.909
I've been saving it.
I wanted you to have it.

00:29:52.952 --> 00:29:58.151
That watch represents a meal,
a hypospray or a pair of boots.

00:29:58.191 --> 00:30:00.591
It could mean the difference
between life and death one day.

00:30:32.926 --> 00:30:34.086
Enter.

00:30:36.462 --> 00:30:38.726
Reporting for duty, Lieutenant.

00:30:38.765 --> 00:30:40.699
What is our agenda?

00:30:40.733 --> 00:30:42.394
After we make
your customary rounds,

00:30:42.435 --> 00:30:44.300
I'd like to take you
to Deflector Control.

00:30:44.337 --> 00:30:47.568
I had an inspiration last night
about the temporal shielding.

00:30:47.607 --> 00:30:48.938
Excellent.

00:30:52.712 --> 00:30:54.202
You've been damaged.

00:30:54.247 --> 00:30:55.714
A minor laceration.

00:30:55.748 --> 00:30:58.581
I've offered to assist you
with your personal grooming.

00:30:58.618 --> 00:31:01.109
There are some tasks I would
rather perform myself.

00:31:01.154 --> 00:31:02.143
Unacceptable.

00:31:02.188 --> 00:31:03.587
You're risking further injury.

00:31:03.623 --> 00:31:06.319
Shaving is hardly
a life-threatening activity.

00:31:08.728 --> 00:31:10.958
Tell me about your inspiration.

00:31:10.997 --> 00:31:13.158
We've been trying
to match our shields

00:31:13.199 --> 00:31:15.531
to the temporal variance
of their torpedoes.

00:31:15.568 --> 00:31:18.230
But I believe we must
also match the deflector array

00:31:18.271 --> 00:31:19.966
to the inverse of that variance.

00:31:20.039 --> 00:31:23.372
Fascinating. When will
the deflectors be ready?

00:31:23.409 --> 00:31:24.376
They're ready now,

00:31:24.410 --> 00:31:26.241
but the modifications
are untested.

00:31:26.279 --> 00:31:28.338
Then our rounds can wait.

00:31:28.381 --> 00:31:30.406
Take me to Deflector Control.

00:31:35.955 --> 00:31:36.922
Seven.

00:31:36.956 --> 00:31:37.980
Ensign.

00:31:38.024 --> 00:31:38.991
A friend of yours?

00:31:39.092 --> 00:31:40.992
My... cabin mate.

00:31:41.094 --> 00:31:43.358
As a Borg, I was accustomed
to cohabitating

00:31:43.396 --> 00:31:45.091
with thousands of other drones.

00:31:45.131 --> 00:31:46.758
But I find it
significantly more difficult

00:31:46.799 --> 00:31:48.323
to live with a single human.

00:31:48.368 --> 00:31:49.494
In what way?

00:31:49.535 --> 00:31:52.003
Ensign Brooks is negligent.

00:31:52.105 --> 00:31:54.266
She leaves her equipment
lying around the quarters

00:31:54.307 --> 00:31:55.831
and her clothing on the floor.

00:31:55.875 --> 00:31:57.740
Indeed. I have found
that most humans

00:31:57.777 --> 00:31:59.005
are less than meticulous

00:31:59.045 --> 00:32:00.945
when it comes
to their domestic habits.

00:32:00.980 --> 00:32:02.311
Indeed.

00:32:02.348 --> 00:32:03.610
Mr. Vulcan, sir.

00:32:03.650 --> 00:32:06.118
A tactical question if I may?

00:32:06.152 --> 00:32:07.210
You may.

00:32:07.253 --> 00:32:08.413
We're just about done

00:32:08.454 --> 00:32:10.649
rebuilding
the internal security sensors

00:32:10.690 --> 00:32:12.851
and we're ready
to program the audio signal.

00:32:12.892 --> 00:32:15.952
Do you want it to say,
"intruder alert"?

00:32:16.062 --> 00:32:18.656
Or should we try something
a little more dramatic

00:32:18.698 --> 00:32:19.790
like "warning, intruder alert"?

00:32:19.832 --> 00:32:22.596
Or..."intruders among us,
danger!

00:32:22.635 --> 00:32:24.159
Danger! Intruders among us"?

00:32:24.203 --> 00:32:26.603
"Intruder alert" will suffice.

00:32:26.639 --> 00:32:28.903
Yeah, go with a classic.

00:32:28.941 --> 00:32:30.169
Understood, sir.

00:32:31.978 --> 00:32:34.003
And you believe
you have difficulties.

00:32:35.214 --> 00:32:36.943
All hands to battle stations.

00:32:36.983 --> 00:32:38.974
Krenim vessels approaching.

00:32:39.085 --> 00:32:41.280
Repeat: All hands
to battle stations!

00:32:41.321 --> 00:32:44.882
Go to Deflector Control and
bring the new shields on line.

00:32:44.924 --> 00:32:46.186
We will test them in battle.

00:33:04.243 --> 00:33:07.212
Computer, activate
tactile interface.

00:33:07.246 --> 00:33:08.679
Weapons status?

00:33:09.849 --> 00:33:11.817
Phasers are still on line.

00:33:11.851 --> 00:33:13.819
Torpedo launchers
are inoperative.

00:33:13.853 --> 00:33:15.684
The Krenim are
within visual range.

00:33:15.722 --> 00:33:17.815
On screen.

00:33:17.857 --> 00:33:19.518
Seven's modified
temporal shields

00:33:19.559 --> 00:33:20.821
should be on line in a moment.

00:33:20.860 --> 00:33:22.452
It's a warship.

00:33:22.495 --> 00:33:24.258
You know the routine.

00:33:24.297 --> 00:33:25.958
Evasive maneuvers.

00:33:27.433 --> 00:33:28.627
They're matching course.

00:33:28.668 --> 00:33:30.363
Hold them off
as long as you can.

00:33:30.403 --> 00:33:31.370
Bridge to Seven of Nine.

00:33:31.404 --> 00:33:32.962
Where are those shields?

00:33:33.039 --> 00:33:34.836
Stand by.

00:33:34.874 --> 00:33:35.966
They're charging weapons.

00:33:36.042 --> 00:33:38.408
Seven, we could use a little

00:33:38.444 --> 00:33:40.412
of that Borg efficiency
right about now.

00:33:40.446 --> 00:33:41.470
I can't shake them off!

00:33:41.514 --> 00:33:43.141
They're targeting the Bridge!

00:33:44.584 --> 00:33:46.381
Temporal shielding is on line.

00:33:46.419 --> 00:33:47.647
They're firing!

00:33:47.687 --> 00:33:49.052
Full port thrusters!

00:33:55.128 --> 00:33:57.460
Temporal shields are holding.

00:33:57.497 --> 00:33:58.521
No damage.

00:33:58.564 --> 00:34:00.998
Hail them.

00:34:01.033 --> 00:34:03.135
Channel open.

00:34:06.538 --> 00:34:09.939
Krenim vessels,
this is the Captain of Voyager.

00:34:10.041 --> 00:34:11.440
You may have noticed

00:34:11.476 --> 00:34:14.536
we have a defense
against your torpedoes now.

00:34:14.579 --> 00:34:16.843
I suggest you stand down.

00:34:20.585 --> 00:34:22.576
No response.

00:34:27.726 --> 00:34:29.956
Their mistake.
Bring the ship about.

00:34:30.061 --> 00:34:33.224
We're going through their space
whether they like it or not.

00:34:45.210 --> 00:34:47.610
We are within range
of the Garenor homeworld.

00:34:48.813 --> 00:34:50.838
Set temporal coordinates.

00:34:52.250 --> 00:34:54.013
Full power to the weapon.

00:34:55.954 --> 00:34:59.720
Prepare for total erasure
of the species.

00:34:59.758 --> 00:35:01.555
Targeting the focal point.

00:35:04.596 --> 00:35:05.995
Ready.

00:35:08.200 --> 00:35:10.259
Fire.

00:35:21.012 --> 00:35:23.105
Temporal incursion in progress.

00:35:23.148 --> 00:35:25.844
Trace elements?

00:35:26.851 --> 00:35:28.148
Diminishing.

00:35:28.186 --> 00:35:29.813
Counter-indications?

00:35:29.854 --> 00:35:31.116
None so far.

00:35:31.156 --> 00:35:34.455
Organisms and structures
are being eradicated.

00:35:35.927 --> 00:35:37.087
Track the temporal wave front

00:35:37.128 --> 00:35:38.459
as it passes
through their system.

00:35:38.496 --> 00:35:43.433
I want to monitor every change
in the timeline as it occurs.

00:35:43.468 --> 00:35:45.629
Yes, sir.

00:35:45.670 --> 00:35:48.161
Captain, the Krenim warship
is in pursuit,

00:35:48.206 --> 00:35:50.197
but their weapons
are not powered.

00:35:50.242 --> 00:35:51.800
Hmm. They don't know
what to do with us

00:35:51.843 --> 00:35:53.811
now that we're shielded
against their torpedoes.

00:35:54.846 --> 00:35:56.245
Captain, there's some kind

00:35:56.281 --> 00:35:58.511
of spatial distortion
heading toward us.

00:35:58.550 --> 00:35:59.847
Sensor readings are erratic.

00:35:59.884 --> 00:36:01.374
I can't identify the phenomenon.

00:36:01.419 --> 00:36:03.284
What's the source?

00:36:03.321 --> 00:36:05.653
Unknown,
but it originated approximately

00:36:05.690 --> 00:36:07.624
20 light-years
from our position.

00:36:07.659 --> 00:36:10.219
It looks like a shock wave
in the fabric of space-time.

00:36:10.262 --> 00:36:11.923
Tom, get us out of here.

00:36:11.997 --> 00:36:14.227
We'll never outrun it, Captain.

00:36:14.266 --> 00:36:15.927
Maybe our new shields will help.

00:36:16.034 --> 00:36:17.626
All hands, brace for impact.

00:36:26.344 --> 00:36:27.743
You were correct, Captain.

00:36:27.779 --> 00:36:30.213
The temporal shielding
has protected us.

00:36:30.248 --> 00:36:32.239
The wave front has passed.

00:36:32.284 --> 00:36:33.273
Captain?

00:36:39.224 --> 00:36:40.384
Report.

00:36:40.425 --> 00:36:41.892
It's definitely a Krenim ship.

00:36:41.926 --> 00:36:44.520
Identical hull markings,
same biospectral frequency...

00:36:44.562 --> 00:36:46.962
but it's half the size.

00:36:47.032 --> 00:36:47.964
Limited fire power.

00:36:48.033 --> 00:36:49.227
What happened to the warship?

00:36:49.267 --> 00:36:51.497
I'm not picking it up
on long-range sensors.

00:36:51.536 --> 00:36:53.595
It looks like
this entire part of space

00:36:53.638 --> 00:36:54.832
has changed somehow.

00:36:54.873 --> 00:36:57.137
The last time I checked,
this region was filled

00:36:57.175 --> 00:36:58.767
with Krenim colonies
and vessels.

00:36:58.810 --> 00:37:01.802
I just ran a scan and
sensors show no colonies

00:37:01.846 --> 00:37:03.643
and just a handful
of Krenim ships.

00:37:03.682 --> 00:37:07.618
Harry, transfer all your sensor
data about that shock wave

00:37:07.652 --> 00:37:09.085
to the Astrometrics Lab.

00:37:09.120 --> 00:37:10.144
Yes, ma'am.

00:37:10.188 --> 00:37:12.156
Tell Seven of Nine
to meet me there.

00:37:12.190 --> 00:37:15.023
Captain, Astrometrics
took heavy damage a few days go.

00:37:15.060 --> 00:37:16.425
It's off-line.

00:37:16.461 --> 00:37:17.928
Well, let's get it back on line.

00:37:17.962 --> 00:37:20.362
It appears that the Krenim
lmperium has vanished.

00:37:20.398 --> 00:37:23.196
Our troubles could be over
and I'd like to find out why.

00:37:26.171 --> 00:37:27.695
Something went wrong.

00:37:27.739 --> 00:37:29.934
The entire Krenim lmperium...

00:37:30.041 --> 00:37:32.305
it's reverted
to a pre-warp state.

00:37:32.344 --> 00:37:34.039
Not possible.

00:37:34.079 --> 00:37:35.478
Our calculations were perfect.

00:37:37.982 --> 00:37:39.847
I may have an explanation.

00:37:39.884 --> 00:37:41.784
There's an anomalous
temporal reading

00:37:41.820 --> 00:37:43.378
20 light-years from here.

00:37:43.421 --> 00:37:45.116
It's coming from a vessel.

00:37:46.558 --> 00:37:48.253
What vessel?

00:37:48.293 --> 00:37:52.389
Component 049-beta,
a ship called Voyager.

00:37:52.430 --> 00:37:55.160
That ship was classified
as an inert component.

00:37:55.200 --> 00:37:57.760
It shouldn't be generating
a temporal field.

00:37:57.802 --> 00:37:59.099
But it is...

00:37:59.137 --> 00:38:01.935
and it was enough to throw
off our calculations.

00:38:04.743 --> 00:38:06.176
Take me to them.

00:38:14.552 --> 00:38:16.383
Sensors are on line.

00:38:19.157 --> 00:38:20.317
Power levels are stable.

00:38:20.358 --> 00:38:22.656
Is the astrometric database
still intact?

00:38:23.762 --> 00:38:24.729
Yes.

00:38:24.763 --> 00:38:26.856
Display the scans
we made of this region

00:38:26.898 --> 00:38:28.525
before the temporal
shock wave hit.

00:38:31.302 --> 00:38:33.532
Spatial grid 005.

00:38:33.571 --> 00:38:38.031
The Krenim lmperium...
over 200 star systems,

00:38:38.076 --> 00:38:39.771
900 planets,

00:38:39.811 --> 00:38:43.645
thousands of warp-capable
vessels and now...

00:38:45.717 --> 00:38:48.447
after the shock wave, everything
seems to have changed.

00:38:48.486 --> 00:38:49.851
Run a new scan.

00:38:52.524 --> 00:38:54.583
Spatial grid 005.

00:38:54.626 --> 00:38:57.094
Same space, different
configuration.

00:38:57.128 --> 00:38:58.959
Exactly as Chakotay said.

00:38:58.997 --> 00:39:01.693
The lmperium
appears to have been reduced

00:39:01.733 --> 00:39:04.702
to a few planets,
and a smattering of vessels.

00:39:06.004 --> 00:39:08.632
It appears that someone...

00:39:08.673 --> 00:39:12.074
or something
has altered history.

00:39:12.110 --> 00:39:14.374
But why weren't we affected?

00:39:14.412 --> 00:39:16.903
Perhaps we were protected
from the changes

00:39:16.981 --> 00:39:18.448
by our temporal shielding.

00:39:18.483 --> 00:39:19.848
Mmm.

00:39:19.884 --> 00:39:21.909
So, the question remains:

00:39:21.953 --> 00:39:25.389
What caused that shock
wave in the first place?

00:39:26.758 --> 00:39:29.454
See if you can track
it back to its origin.

00:39:29.494 --> 00:39:33.487
The shock wave emanated from
a planet 20 light-years away.

00:39:33.531 --> 00:39:35.396
The Garenor homeworld.

00:39:35.433 --> 00:39:36.627
The Garenor?

00:39:36.668 --> 00:39:38.295
We passed their planet
three weeks ago.

00:39:40.839 --> 00:39:43.069
The planet
is no longer populated.

00:39:43.107 --> 00:39:45.200
What?

00:39:45.243 --> 00:39:47.643
Astrometric data indicate

00:39:47.679 --> 00:39:49.772
that the instant
the shock wave appeared,

00:39:49.814 --> 00:39:52.476
the Garenor species vanished.

00:39:54.786 --> 00:39:57.254
Erased from history.

00:39:58.723 --> 00:39:59.849
Captain?

00:40:01.559 --> 00:40:03.083
I'm no authority on time travel.

00:40:03.127 --> 00:40:05.960
In fact, I've made it my goal
in life to avoid it, but...

00:40:09.167 --> 00:40:12.330
this sounds to me like
a causality paradox.

00:40:12.370 --> 00:40:14.065
Think about it.

00:40:14.105 --> 00:40:18.405
A temporal shock wave
eliminates a single species

00:40:18.443 --> 00:40:21.742
and all of history
changes as a result.

00:40:23.047 --> 00:40:25.607
An intriguing theory.

00:40:25.650 --> 00:40:27.618
Perhaps the Krenim
are responsible.

00:40:27.652 --> 00:40:29.711
They do possess
temporal technology.

00:40:29.754 --> 00:40:32.279
But why would they alter history
to undermine themselves?

00:40:32.323 --> 00:40:35.315
No, we're still missing
a big piece of the puzzle.

00:40:35.360 --> 00:40:36.622
Run another scan of the...

00:40:43.635 --> 00:40:45.125
Scanning the vessel.

00:40:45.169 --> 00:40:46.466
Their defensive shielding

00:40:46.504 --> 00:40:48.870
is generating a level-9
temporal disruption.

00:40:48.907 --> 00:40:49.999
Collect samples...

00:40:50.074 --> 00:40:52.599
two life-forms,
ten square meters of the hull.

00:40:52.644 --> 00:40:54.009
Yes, sir.

00:40:54.045 --> 00:40:55.740
Disable their shielding.

00:40:55.780 --> 00:40:58.476
Prepare to initiate
a temporal incursion.

00:41:00.451 --> 00:41:02.783
That entire vessel's
in a state of temporal flux.

00:41:02.820 --> 00:41:05.812
It's like they exist
outside space-time.

00:41:05.857 --> 00:41:07.791
They're scanning us.

00:41:09.727 --> 00:41:11.126
Get a lock on them!

00:41:11.162 --> 00:41:13.858
I'm trying, but I can't
isolate their signals.

00:41:13.898 --> 00:41:15.058
We are being hailed.

00:41:15.099 --> 00:41:16.191
On screen.

00:41:18.002 --> 00:41:19.799
State your identity.

00:41:19.837 --> 00:41:22.863
I'm Captain Janeway of the
Federation Starship Voyager.

00:41:22.907 --> 00:41:24.704
Who are you,
and where are my men?

00:41:24.742 --> 00:41:26.573
I am Annorax
of the Krenim lmperium.

00:41:26.611 --> 00:41:28.841
We've transferred your crewmen
to my vessel

00:41:28.880 --> 00:41:30.370
for further analysis.

00:41:30.415 --> 00:41:33.578
Your ship does not come
from this Quadrant.

00:41:33.618 --> 00:41:38.351
We come from Earth... a planet
65,000 light-years from here.

00:41:38.389 --> 00:41:40.118
We're on our way home.

00:41:40.158 --> 00:41:41.785
I see.

00:41:41.826 --> 00:41:43.418
We've been observing
some rather...

00:41:43.461 --> 00:41:46.453
unusual events in the region.

00:41:46.497 --> 00:41:48.795
It seems your lmperium...

00:41:48.833 --> 00:41:49.800
never existed.

00:41:49.834 --> 00:41:52.268
Perhaps you could shed
some light on this.

00:41:52.303 --> 00:41:53.998
That doesn't concern you.

00:41:54.105 --> 00:41:57.302
What is important
is that you understand

00:41:57.342 --> 00:41:59.810
that I bear you no hostility...

00:41:59.844 --> 00:42:02.404
but you have diverted me
from my mission.

00:42:02.447 --> 00:42:03.971
Your mission?

00:42:07.518 --> 00:42:10.749
You're responsible
for the changes in the timeline.

00:42:10.788 --> 00:42:12.779
You're a long way
from your world.

00:42:12.824 --> 00:42:16.726
In a manner of speaking,
so am I.

00:42:16.761 --> 00:42:20.754
Unfortunately, only one of us
can go home again.

00:42:20.798 --> 00:42:23.528
Your sacrifice will restore
the lives

00:42:23.568 --> 00:42:25.934
of countless millions.

00:42:25.970 --> 00:42:28.097
I'm sorry.

00:42:29.807 --> 00:42:31.604
I'm reading a massive
energy buildup...

00:42:31.643 --> 00:42:32.610
some kind of weapon.

00:42:32.644 --> 00:42:33.941
Shields.

00:42:39.851 --> 00:42:42.149
Temporal shields are weakening.

00:42:42.186 --> 00:42:43.915
Captain, that energy beam...

00:42:43.955 --> 00:42:45.820
it's pushing Voyager
out of the space-time continuum.

00:42:45.857 --> 00:42:48.826
He's trying to erase us
from history.

00:42:48.860 --> 00:42:51.158
I have scanned
their propulsion system.

00:42:51.195 --> 00:42:54.494
Their vessel's mass prevents
them from exceeding warp 6.

00:42:54.532 --> 00:42:56.227
We can escape.

00:42:56.267 --> 00:42:57.393
Captain, I must remind you,

00:42:57.435 --> 00:43:00.199
our structural integrity
is still impaired.

00:43:00.238 --> 00:43:01.262
If we go to warp now,

00:43:01.305 --> 00:43:03.239
the damage to Voyager
will be extreme.

00:43:03.274 --> 00:43:04.901
What about Tom and Chakotay?

00:43:04.942 --> 00:43:06.569
We'll have to come back
for them.

00:43:06.611 --> 00:43:08.408
All hands
clear the outer sections

00:43:08.446 --> 00:43:10.414
and prepare
for wide-scale breaches.

00:43:10.448 --> 00:43:14.009
Tuvok, activate
the transverse bulkheads.

00:43:16.187 --> 00:43:18.348
Temporal shields are failing.

00:43:18.389 --> 00:43:19.856
Engage warp 7.

00:43:20.958 --> 00:43:22.016
They're not in pursuit.

00:43:24.028 --> 00:43:25.290
We are losing the outer hull.

00:43:25.329 --> 00:43:26.762
Transverse bulkheads
are holding.

00:43:38.276 --> 00:43:40.244
Each of you has done your best,

00:43:40.278 --> 00:43:41.677
but determination alone

00:43:41.713 --> 00:43:43.874
isn't going to hold
this ship together.

00:43:43.915 --> 00:43:46.349
It's time we faced reality.

00:43:46.384 --> 00:43:49.478
We've lost nine decks.

00:43:49.520 --> 00:43:52.387
More than half the ship
has been destroyed.

00:43:52.423 --> 00:43:55.392
Life support is nearly gone.

00:43:55.426 --> 00:43:59.522
Voyager can no longer
sustain its crew.

00:43:59.564 --> 00:44:02.556
I promised myself that I
would never give this order,

00:44:02.600 --> 00:44:05.034
that I would never break up
this family,

00:44:05.069 --> 00:44:06.866
but asking you to stay...

00:44:09.340 --> 00:44:12.309
would be asking you to die.

00:44:12.343 --> 00:44:13.674
You will proceed

00:44:13.711 --> 00:44:16.373
to the escape pods,
and evacuate this vessel.

00:44:16.414 --> 00:44:18.439
Set your course
for the Alpha Quadrant.

00:44:18.483 --> 00:44:21.247
Along the way,
try to find allies.

00:44:21.285 --> 00:44:22.946
Secure faster ships if you can.

00:44:23.020 --> 00:44:24.817
Anything to get home.

00:44:24.856 --> 00:44:25.823
The senior staff and I

00:44:25.857 --> 00:44:27.586
will remain on board
as long as possible.

00:44:27.625 --> 00:44:31.425
We will try, somehow,
to rescue Tom and Chakotay.

00:44:31.462 --> 00:44:34.761
The escape pods are equipped
with subspace beacons.

00:44:34.799 --> 00:44:36.426
That's how we'll keep track
of you.

00:44:36.467 --> 00:44:39.300
When we find each other again...

00:44:39.337 --> 00:44:41.498
and we will...

00:44:41.539 --> 00:44:44.906
we will find each other again...

00:44:44.942 --> 00:44:47.968
I expect all of you
to be in one piece

00:44:48.045 --> 00:44:51.071
with some interesting stories
to tell.

00:44:54.051 --> 00:44:55.575
Good luck.
